Kitab \(|f(2.6133)| = 0.0072\) par ruk kar ise 0.01 ke barabar maan leti hai, lekin us ka apna rule (8.3.1) 2 decimal places ke liye \(|f(c)| < 0.005\) hai, aur 0.0072 is se bara hai. Teen iterations aur karne se shart poori hoti hai:
9: \(c = 2.6114\), \(f(c) = -0.0260\), interval \([2.6114, 2.6133]\);
10: \(c = 2.6124\), \(f(c) = -0.0085\), interval \([2.6124, 2.6133]\);
11: \(c = 2.6129\), \(f(c) = 0.0002 < 0.005\): ab rukein.
Aakhri root \(x \approx 2.61\) wahi rehta hai.
